.TH "SPGEN-COMMAND" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-command \- Generates a command module, its test and router registration
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.command [options] <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The intent to change an aggregate, validated before it is dispatched.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the command, its data, its publishes events and its constraints, and the aggregate's invariants.
.SH "What the generator does"
.IP \[bu] 2
Struct from the command's data: use TypedStruct, use ExConstructor, enforce: true per required field, never struct\-level.
.IP \[bu] 2
use Vex.Struct plus one validates line per required field and per resolved rule, with the validator alias.
.IP \[bu] 2
The rules themselves: a unique\-<field> invariant or an <domain\-object>\-exists constraint brings the validator (./validator.md), the internal API accessor it calls, the lookup query behind that accessor and the read model that query reads — all in the same run.
.IP \[bu] 2
@moduledoc describing what the command does to the aggregate, and @doc for new/1 — from the model's description, or a TODO: marker where the model is silent.
.IP \[bu] 2
Registration: identify/dispatch in the composite's commanded router, and that router in the subdomain's commanded application. Both files are created when the composite or subdomain lacks one.
.SH Tests
In the operation test (./operation\-test.md), under describe "Command": requires id, id cannot be nil, and validates presence of <field> for every required field. The invariant cases are still manual — see Known gaps (../../README.md#known\-gaps) — and assert the error the example (./examples/unique\-slug.md) states ({:error, :slug_exists}), never a second convention.
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>/command.ex (typedstruct command with enforces)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/validators/<_validator>.ex (Vex rules per invariant)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/operations/<_operation>_test.exs (enforced field validation tests)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/router.ex (dispatch and middleware registration)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/application.ex (application router registration)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
what the operation does: create|update|delete|none (optional: the model declares the operation for this element)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
create
.IP \(bu 2
update
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.IP \(bu 2
none
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
